WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.667
-Our next guest
is a talented actress

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:03.767
you know from her work in shows

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:05.167
such as "The Knick"
and "Bad Sisters."

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:07.300
She stars in the film
"Flora and Son,"

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.033
which is streaming now
on Apple TV+.

00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:10.367
Let's take a look.

00:00:10.367 --> 00:00:14.300
-I do intend to learn the
guitar and take it seriously.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.901
Why? I don't know.

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:20.000
I was always the one in class
making fun of the teacher

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.467
because someone had to.

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:25.767
But I won't if you'll
keep teaching me.

00:00:25.767 --> 00:00:28.067
Sorry I objectified you.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:30.167
I can send you a picture
of my amazing tits

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:33.567
to balance things out again,
if you'd like.

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:34.834
Flora.

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:39.534
[ Camera shutter clicks ]

00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:41.200
[ Cellphone swishes ]

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.634
Right. Now let's get
that [bleep] off your arse.

00:00:44.634 --> 00:00:48.100
-Please welcome back to the show
Eve Hewson, everybody.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:02.334 --> 00:01:03.567
Welcome back.

00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:05.734
-Thank you. It's so good to be
here, finally.

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:07.567
-It's a thrill to have you.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:10.467
You -- This is a wonderful film
about a young mother

00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:12.267
who connects with a troubled son

00:01:12.267 --> 00:01:15.234
by learning to play guitar
and singing music.

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:17.534
I've heard you are afraid
of singing in public.

00:01:17.534 --> 00:01:19.200
-Terrified.
-Always.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.434
-This is not for me.

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:22.534
This was not my plan
in life to sing.

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:24.300
-But you can sing.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:27.767
-No, I...
I can, like...

00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:29.267
♪ Eeh-dee-dee-dee-dee-dee ♪

00:01:29.267 --> 00:01:31.267
-Okay, so I take it back.
You can't, yeah.

00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:32.901
-I sound --
I think, in the film,

00:01:32.901 --> 00:01:35.634
I sound like
a tiny baby chipmunk

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:36.934
with, like,
a dagger at its back,

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:38.267
like, "Sing, sing."

00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:39.701
And I'm like...
[ Vocalizes ]

00:01:39.701 --> 00:01:42.367
-But, now, do the other people
feel like you sound that way

00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:44.234
or do you think
that's only through your ears?

00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:47.400
-I read a review where they
said I sang like an angel.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.667
-Oh!

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:52.734
-And I sent it immediately
to my singing teacher.

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:54.734
-Oh, that's good.
-I was like, "What did we do?

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:56.167
How did this happen?"

00:01:56.167 --> 00:01:57.400
-The singing teacher was like,

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:58.667
"I am going to put that
on my business card."

00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:00.634
-Absolutely. He's -- Yeah.

00:02:00.634 --> 00:02:03.334
-So, but you actually --
This is a very real fear.

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:06.367
There were times in your career
where if you had to sing

00:02:06.367 --> 00:02:08.968
in an audition,
you would just --

00:02:08.968 --> 00:02:10.167
-I would leave.
-You would just beat it.

00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:11.334
-Anytime I'd read a script

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:13.267
and the the character
would start singing,

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:14.400
I was like, "Ooh, sorry.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.234
Can't do it. You know, busy."

00:02:17.234 --> 00:02:18.868
-Nothing must have been worse
than if you read

00:02:18.868 --> 00:02:21.200
a whole screenplay,
and only at the very end

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.100
did your character sing,
and you were like --

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.767
-That's how I felt
actually reading this script,

00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:27.534
because it was so funny
and it was so good.

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:30.400
And I was like, "Please
no singing, please no singing."

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:33.400
And then I got halfway through
and I was like, "Oh, God!"

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:36.934
No, but I had --
I auditioned for "La La Land,"

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:39.601
which everybody knows
"La La Land."

00:02:39.601 --> 00:02:41.367
-Came this close to winning
the Oscar.

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:43.968
-It did.

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:47.467
And thank God
I'm not in it, you know?

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:48.734
But, basically, I went in,
and they were like,

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:51.000
"Okay, so, you're meeting
with Damien Chazelle,

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.567
and it's kind of
an improv-y thing."

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:54.501
And I was like, "Oh, improv.
Fine. Like, I'll go in.

00:02:54.501 --> 00:02:55.767
I like that stuff."

00:02:55.767 --> 00:02:59.400
So, I go in -- joke, joke, joke,
charm, charm, charm.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.367
And Damien is like, "Ha ha ha."

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:02.801
And I leave.

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:05.501
And my agent calls me
and she's like,

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:07.167
"Oh, my God, he loves you.

00:03:07.167 --> 00:03:08.501
He thinks you're great.

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:10.701
And you have to go back in now
for your second audition.

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:12.133
It's the singing."

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:15.601
And I was like, "No."

00:03:15.601 --> 00:03:16.868
-You big-timed him.

00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:20.200
-I literally was like,
"I'm absolutely not going.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.501
Like, there's nothing
you could say."

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.667
And they were like,
"This could be an Oscar movie.

00:03:24.667 --> 00:03:26.367
It's very big for your career."

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:28.267
I was like, "Absolutely not
going to happen."

00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:30.200
-That must be so funny
as an agent to, like,

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:31.501
hang up the phone and be like,

00:03:31.501 --> 00:03:32.968
"I think we have
a terrible client."

00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:36.868
-I know. She was
so frustrated with me.

00:03:36.868 --> 00:03:39.300
And I also wasn't getting a lot
of work at the time either,

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.434
so it was like --

00:03:40.434 --> 00:03:42.234
-I like that you stood
on ceremony there

00:03:42.234 --> 00:03:43.567
and I like that it worked out.

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:46.667
I also -- I have to say,
"Bad Sisters"

00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:48.000
was one of my favorite shows
of recent years.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.968
-Thank you. Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:51.300
Yeah!

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:54.467
Like this film,
it took place in Dublin.

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:57.434
And I wanted to ask,
because there's sort of

00:03:57.434 --> 00:03:58.701
a big part of the film
is that everybody --

00:03:58.701 --> 00:04:00.567
-Yes.
-What is it called, again?

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:02.334
-It's called the Forty Foot.
-The Forty Foot.

00:04:02.334 --> 00:04:04.067
And it's sort of jumping off
into the water.

00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:05.367
And had you ever done it as a --

00:04:05.367 --> 00:04:07.567
-Yeah, I grew up five minutes
away from there.

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:09.167
-And so you had
actually done it before?

00:04:09.167 --> 00:04:10.267
-I had done it before,

00:04:10.267 --> 00:04:11.934
but I sort of --
To prep for the show,

00:04:11.934 --> 00:04:13.133
I was doing it every day.

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:15.033
-Gotcha.
-And --

00:04:15.033 --> 00:04:16.767
-To prep for the fear
of jumping off?

00:04:16.767 --> 00:04:17.934
What's the worst part --

00:04:17.934 --> 00:04:19.501
-No, you have to get
your body temperature

00:04:19.501 --> 00:04:21.033
into a certain place
or else you'll die.

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:22.667
-Gotcha.

00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:23.801
-Yeah.
-That's great.

00:04:23.801 --> 00:04:24.901
-And it was funny
because the other --

00:04:24.901 --> 00:04:26.100
-That's why
a lot of people don't take

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.701
spring-break trips to Dublin.

00:04:27.701 --> 00:04:29.100
-Yeah.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.000
-They should.
-They should, yeah.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.133
-The other girls were like,

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:34.033
"I just don't think
this is going to be safe

00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:35.167
and I don't think
we should do it."

00:04:35.167 --> 00:04:36.767
I was like,
"Guys, the whole show

00:04:36.767 --> 00:04:37.901
is based around this location."

00:04:37.901 --> 00:04:39.467
-Yeah, it culminates with
this moment, yeah.

00:04:39.467 --> 00:04:40.567
-We have to do it.

00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:42.334
So, when we got there,
they were like,

00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:44.100
"Oh, no, you're just going to
jump off the steps."

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:45.300
And I was like, "I've been
practicing jumping off

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.467
the cliff.

00:04:46.467 --> 00:04:48.501
I must do the cliff."
So I did the cliff.

00:04:48.501 --> 00:04:50.100
-And did the rest of your cast
do the cliff?

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.701
-Nope.
-Yeah.

00:04:51.701 --> 00:04:53.767
Well, I'm glad
we made it very clear here

00:04:53.767 --> 00:04:55.767
that that was all stunt doubles
except for you.

00:04:55.767 --> 00:04:57.400
You were the real deal.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.434
You received --
Early in your career,

00:04:59.434 --> 00:05:00.767
you've worked
with some great actors.

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:02.334
You received
-Oh, gosh.

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:05.033
-From one of my favorite actors,

00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:08.868
you received a note
about something you did well,

00:05:08.868 --> 00:05:10.067
that you've continued
to do well.

00:05:10.067 --> 00:05:11.868
So, this is the original, yes?

00:05:11.868 --> 00:05:14.801
-There I am.
-Okay. And who was the actor?

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:17.501
-I worked -- One of
the first movies I did,

00:05:17.501 --> 00:05:20.334
I was 20 years old and I played
James Gandolfini's daughter.

00:05:20.334 --> 00:05:22.701
-The great James Gandolfini.
-In "Enough Said."

00:05:22.701 --> 00:05:26.167
And we did a scene --

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:29.801
Myself, James Gandolfini,
and Julia Louis-Dreyfus.

00:05:29.801 --> 00:05:34.501
And we were eating lunch,
and I just demolished the salad.

00:05:34.501 --> 00:05:35.634
in every take.

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:39.100
And afterwards, he was like,

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:42.968
"This is the greatest
acting I've ever seen."

00:05:42.968 --> 00:05:46.167
You know, coming from the king
of eating on camera.

00:05:46.167 --> 00:05:47.400
He invented it.
-Yes, I was gonna say.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:50.000
The great eating actor
of our time.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.300
-So, he was like, "I love you.
You're the best.

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:56.400
I hate seeing these actors.
They're..."

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.734
And so he was like,
"Keep doing that."

00:05:58.734 --> 00:05:59.801
-And you have.

00:05:59.801 --> 00:06:03.634
-I have every time,
in every movie.

00:06:03.634 --> 00:06:06.534
As a tribute to Jim.

00:06:06.534 --> 00:06:09.501
-There you go. Just everywhere.

00:06:09.501 --> 00:06:11.601
Just chowing down.
-All the time.

00:06:11.601 --> 00:06:14.767
And it is a tribute to Jim, but
very quickly, like, there --

00:06:14.767 --> 00:06:17.801
-I'm also hungry,
but it's also a tribute to Jim.

00:06:17.801 --> 00:06:19.133
-But there are,
of course, people on set

00:06:19.133 --> 00:06:21.334
who probably would prefer you
to do the tiny nibble.

00:06:21.334 --> 00:06:22.968
-Yeah, the props department
were like, "Oh, my God.

00:06:22.968 --> 00:06:24.067
Here we go."

00:06:24.067 --> 00:06:25.534
And even when we were
shooting "Flora,"

00:06:25.534 --> 00:06:27.868
John Carney, our director,
was like, "Oh, my God.

00:06:27.868 --> 00:06:29.367
You're really eating
that spaghetti."

00:06:29.367 --> 00:06:31.367
I was like, "Of course I am."
-I love it.

00:06:31.367 --> 00:06:33.868
They're like -- Like, both
props and budget is like,

00:06:33.868 --> 00:06:35.200
"We are over our
spaghetti budget.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:37.300
-I know.
-"We can't afford this."

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:39.133
-"We can't hire Eve Hewson.

00:06:39.133 --> 00:06:41.100
The spaghetti budget
goes way up."

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:44.801
-She won't sing and she eats
all the spaghetti.

00:06:44.801 --> 00:06:46.334
Congratulations
on this beautiful film.

00:06:46.334 --> 00:06:47.734
And it's so lovely
to see you again.

00:06:47.734 --> 00:06:48.767
Thanks for being here.
-Thank you so much.

00:06:48.767 --> 00:06:50.033
-Eve Hewson, everybody.

00:06:50.033 --> 00:06:52.133
"Flora and Son" is streaming
now on Apple TV+.

00:06:52.133 --> 00:06:53.634
We'll be right back
with Ari Melber.

